{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgRzPmkjoSj4zMorZCZ9K","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I split the system prompt into two cached blocks in `build_system` (`bot.py`), so a `save_fact` no longer rewrites the instructions' cache entry. I couldn't call the API here, so I haven't seen the cache numbers change. Whether it works depends on the 1024-token caching minimum for Sonnet 4.5, which the static block may not reach.\n\n- **Cause:** the instructions and the per-user context (date, profile, zones, goal, facts) shared one block with one `cache_control` marker. A new fact changed the hash of the whole block, so the next call re-created the whole prompt.\n- **Fix:** block one is `INSTRUCTIONS`, which has no per-user or per-day text in it. Block two is `athlete_context(...)`. Each has its own `cache_control: ephemeral` marker.\n- **Local check:** after adding a fact, block one is byte-identical and block two differs.\n- **Left alone:** I kept the keyword-based tool filtering, since `NOTES.md` says to. I didn't add per-message fact selection either, because it would make the second block miss on every message.\n- **Colleague's note:** I used the two-marker split, the byte-stability rule and the \"include all facts\" rule. The ~55 tools, MCP setup and token sizes don't apply to this bot. `ANSWER.md` says this.\n- **Risk to check after deploy:** the log suggests the static prefix (core tools plus instructions) is only about 800–950 tokens. If it is under 1024, the first marker creates no cache entry on its own. Behaviour would then be no worse than before, but a memory write would still cause a full miss.\n- **How to tell:** send two messages, trigger a `save_fact`, then send a third. If the third call's `cache_creation_input_tokens` is the size of the full prompt, the prefix is under the minimum.\n- **Possible follow-up:** always send all tools. That adds about 150 tokens, keeps the tools array stable and gets the prefix over 1024, but it undoes the filtering. I left that decision to you."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1935,"cache_read_input_tokens":28800,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1935},"output_tokens":673,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d696f52c-4d5c-4867-bcb0-ffa94643a83a","uuid":"e46560df-874d-48d2-982f-bd63e57f9ed2","timestamp":"2026-10-27T02:56:51.658Z","request_id":"req_011CgRzPmU8BJA5ZLpReMbRR"}
